  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a user, I want the app to reopen on the same forum, topic, page and position, also after folding or app switching, so that I never lose my place.\n\n### Scope\n\nScene storage of selection and reading position; sidebar visibility kept; no empty detail pane after switching apps.\n\n- Module: App · Difficulty: medium · Priority: medium · post-MVP\n- Implements: FEAT-015 (#159)\n- Absorbs: FEAT-015; user feedback iPad state handling (p. 507-509)\n- Legacy sources (read-only, `origin/master`): `MainWindow.swift` (`SidebarVisibilityStorage`, `RuntimeState`), legacy HFR-007\n- Spec: `docs/features/FEAT-015.md` (feature spec, ADR 0011 §2; write it first if absent, crediting Bybifok) plus a short `docs/lots/LOT-145-*.md` pointing to it\n\n### Depends on\n\n- LOT-090 (#182, done)\n- LOT-082 (#100, done)\n- LOT-083 (#101, done)\n\n### On hold\n\nHeld by the M5_OPEN decision: M5 opens after the M4 parity is validated, and the orchestrator opens it (operator decisions of 2026-11-02 on #379). ([decision](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/issues/379#issuecomment-6573879240))\n\n### Feature umbrella\n\n- Implements FEAT-015 (#159), proposed by Bybifok (credit in the spec, PR and CREDITS.md). Other lots of this feature: LOT-090 (#182); **this lot is the last one: its PR also says `Closes #159`**.\n\nFEAT issues (#145–#165) are umbrellas and are never claimed: claim this lot's issue; the PR says `Closes #<this issue>` and `Refs #<FEAT issue>`.\n\n### Model\n\nOpus → Fable (AGENTS.md §6: the reviewer is never the author model)\n\n### Captures needed\n\n- none known; any page state the spec needs and the fixtures lack is listed as *pending capture*, never hand-built (LESSONS 35-36)\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Scenario of p. 508 (category → topic → app switch → back) restores the topic (UI test or model test).\n- [ ] View logic lives in `@Observable @MainActor` models tested with Swift Testing in `App/SwiftHFRTests/`; each new test is shown to fail without the change.\n- [ ] `xcodebuild build test` green on the iPhone 18 Pro and an iPad simulator (iOS 27.0), and the `App build + tests` CI job green.\n- [ ] UI strings in French; light, dark and Dynamic Type XL checked; no new dependency; no HFR fact without a source (legacy file:line or fixture).\n\n### Before you start (agents and humans)\n\nRead, in order: AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, docs/agents/ORCHESTRATION.md, docs/agents/REVIEW-ROUNDS.md, docs/agents/LESSONS.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, App/README.md, ADR 0012, the spec of every dependency (docs/lots/), docs/HFR-PROTOCOL.md for any forum fact, docs/FIXTURES.md if captures are involved. Claim with `/claim <session-id>` on this issue before writing code; PR body `Closes #<this issue>` + `Claim: <session-id>`; never guess HFR behaviour (stop and list the captures needed).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
